{"title":"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rounded to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> decimal places, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/733160f5f247da3bbd58f674a035949cd723f151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f093f3f8b47cf6e7246ad8f7ecdbf0746c774c87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 0.70 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 0.77 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 0.78 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 0.79 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 0.80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"504\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34d9f410f408513f370857eefbe863d389eb045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac79 = 0.\\overline{777}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Rounding this number to the nearest hundredth (to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> decimal places), we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ec1604985cb839e1f7c515ec1020fbff8cd7e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 0.78}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" /> because the thousandths place is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so it is closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132cf35020c5f49c07cb65da01ac1cc1a57af626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd4b2eb693f3ec8b9880bf27cd9420b52caecb93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can go backwards by multiplying answer choices by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and seeing how they compare to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132cf35020c5f49c07cb65da01ac1cc1a57af626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/83521a39925f75859c4a7e8f1d8edb33fde44a2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.78 \\times 9 = 7.02$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>This makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace1481f3632164fea0f41af593f0014e518cb90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a1915ca58d8d7796558f721032b45266148e68d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> too large and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/8/058d75a079a31d25626e88bdb171c7d9b37e24b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> too small, eliminating them as answers\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb911da8ccf1749df2a3aa6602189b3b418de2a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.77 \\times 9 = 6.93$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can now look at which answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is closest to, using the distance to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419511bc1ec09a4b73e1eaac814c88d46624564d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 6.93 = 0.07$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca8902b22e2a709880c3f1d947069f095e00cf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.02 - 7 = 0.02$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42496e2c2d6aaf881b1775020ba17c88c9434b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.02$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> is closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ec1604985cb839e1f7c515ec1020fbff8cd7e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 0.78}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</t